# Production vs artifacts

| Kind | Location |
|------|----------|
| Service production code | `src/VectorNNTPD.BackFillerService/` |
| Shared library production code | `src/VectorNNTPD.Common/` |
| Service tests | `tests/VectorNNTPD.BackFillerService.Tests/` |
| Shared library tests | `tests/VectorNNTPD.Common.Tests/` |
| Permanent docs (explicitly accepted only) | `docs/` |
| Local experiments, benches, audits, generated reports, prototypes | `.artifacts/` |
| Local release staging | `.artifacts/release/win-64` and `.artifacts/release/linux-64` |
| CI Native AOT publish output | `.artifacts/win-x64` and `.artifacts/linux-x64` on the runner |

`.gitignore` ignores `.artifacts/`. `tools/Publish-Release.ps1` and `.github/workflows/build.yml` write repository-controlled publish output there. `actions/upload-artifact` uploads those directories; the action does not require the local directory to be named `artifacts/`. Release staging is `.artifacts/release/` and does not replace `.artifacts/articles` or existing benchmark reports.

Agents write local evidence under `.artifacts/`. Do not put committable documentation or policy there: the directory is gitignored, so a file created only to satisfy an old index path will not be in git. This rule is the committed placement policy. There is no committed `.artifacts/ARTIFACT-INDEX.md` or `.artifacts/REPOSITORY-ARTIFACT-POLICY.md`.

If unsure a document is permanent: write it under `.artifacts/` when it is disposable local evidence. Never default to `docs/SOMETHING.md`.

Do not put experimental/benchmark/prototype/diagnostic code under `src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, or `tools/` unless the user explicitly promotes it.

Promotion (`.artifacts/` → `docs/` or `src/`/`tests/`) requires an explicit user decision.

## Source of truth

1. Current `src/`
2. Current `tests/`
3. Accepted `docs/`
4. `.artifacts/` (local evidence only, when present on disk)

Before command or data-plane work: inspect production code, then accepted `docs/`. Local files under `.artifacts/` are evidence from a machine, not current architecture.

Do not delete or “clean up” historical artifacts. Do not implement features or optimize as part of indexing/hygiene tasks. Do not write new repository output under `artifacts/`.
